WEBVTT

00:04:28.708 --> 00:04:32.018
because if you knew which person
had a little bit more authority

00:04:32.042 --> 00:04:33.643
or more influence,

00:04:33.667 --> 00:04:35.851
then the structure was stable.

00:04:35.875 --> 00:04:37.768
It was consistent, it was predictable,

00:04:37.792 --> 00:04:41.643
whereas if people had equal power,
they were constantly jocking for position,

00:04:41.667 --> 00:04:44.976
and it wasn't clear
where anyone should stand.

00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:49.434
And it seems like that dynamic
is more common in romantic relationships

00:04:49.458 --> 00:04:51.434
than it is in professional relationships.

00:04:51.458 --> 00:04:53.518
Because at work
we have hierarchies, right?

00:04:53.542 --> 00:04:54.809
We know who the boss is.

00:04:54.833 --> 00:04:57.601
We often know, if not,
who has power in a team,

00:04:57.625 --> 00:05:00.684
who has more status
or who has more accomplishments.